preConditionHook:
// EL: ovBar = minlist(h[kk], h[kk+1]) - maxlist(l[kk], l[kk+1]), clamped at 0,
//     ovSum accumulated as ovBar / (h[kk+1] - l[kk+1] + epsilon),
//     ovAvg = ovSum / lookback.
// MinList/MaxList are ACCEPTED for tick-grid PRICE operands only
// (EL_FEATURES.md): these operands are bar extremes, so they differ by exactly
// 0 or by at least one tick -- 1e9-1e11x the relational tolerance -- and
// whichever comparison the reserved word carries cannot matter. The plain
// ternary stand-in is therefore exact, the same arrangement BarOverlapFraction
// and AtrProfitTarget use. (<algorithm> is not among the emitted includes, so
// no std::min/std::max.)
// The gap clamp is written as an EL if-clamp rather than maxlist(0, ...)
// because 0 against a price DIFFERENCE is a computed operand, outside
// minlist/maxlist's ACCEPTED scope; an ordinary EL relational is VERIFIED and
// carries the measured tolerance. Same reasoning as BarOverlapFraction.
// The epsilon guards a zero-range reference bar: EL raises a runtime
// divide-by-zero error on a zero denominator (EL_FEATURES.md), so it is an
// input rather than a nicety.
// The accumulation order is oldest-index-last, matching the EL loop statement
// for statement; a mean of ratios is not associative in floating point.
ovSum = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    ovBar = (high[i] < high[i + 1] ? high[i] : high[i + 1])
            - (low[i] > low[i + 1] ? low[i] : low[i + 1]);
    if (el_lt(ovBar, 0.0)) ovBar = 0.0;
    ovSum = ovSum + ovBar / (high[i + 1] - low[i + 1] + epsilon);
}
ovAvg = ovSum / lookback;
